  "summary": "Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu publicly celebrated the dismissal of the International Criminal Court prosecutor, calling the outcome a \"con job\". The development follows a prolonged dispute over an arrest warrant, according to reporting by the TOI World Desk.",
  "content": "'Con job': Netanyahu celebrates ICC prosecutor's dismissal after arrest warrant battle\n\nIsraeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu celebrated the dismissal of the International Criminal Court's prosecutor, describing the outcome as a \"con job,\" according to the report headline. The development comes after a prolonged legal and political battle centered on an arrest warrant that had drawn international attention and debate.\n\nCoverage by the TOI World Desk said its team of journalists and writers followed the unfolding story and offered ongoing updates and perspectives. The outlet emphasized its commitment to accuracy and depth as it tracked reactions and implications from across the globe.\n\nDetails in the report are limited: the article notes the dismissal and Netanyahu's response but provides few specifics about the legal reasoning, statements from the ICC itself, or the broader international reaction. The author and exact publication details were listed as unknown in the provided material. Observers of international justice and diplomacy will likely watch for official statements from the ICC and responses from other governments and legal experts as the situation develops.",
